      "scope": "Consultation method: direct_page_selected_passages_via_web_open. Section: Borrowed noun and historical mining vocabulary. Metal came through French and Latin from Greek vocabulary related to mining. The history does not create a current met-plus-al analysis. The material base can be reused in sheet metal and related compounds without collapsing their completed lexical identities. Limits: Selected lexical and historical passages only. No dictionary examples, full text, media or source exercises are acquired. These paraphrases support a proposed teaching-depth decision; they do not establish independent morphology acceptance, specialist approval, product composition, handling instructions, media licensing or course readiness.",
