      "scope": "Consultation method: direct_page_selected_passages_via_web_open. Section: Thin wrapping-paper noun and first attestation. The two-word noun denotes very thin paper used in wrapping and related delicate applications. Its present spelling and packaging meaning support two ordered whole constituents with one word boundary. It is not a biological-tissue phrase or an instruction to use any facial tissue for packaging. Limits: Selected lexical and historical passages only. No dictionary examples, full text, media or source exercises are acquired. These paraphrases support a proposed teaching-depth decision; they do not establish independent morphology acceptance, specialist approval, product composition, handling instructions, media licensing or course readiness.",
